# README — Source Data: Ex Vivo Cytokine Discovery vs. Validation 4-Quadrant Plots

## Overview
This file contains the regression results underlying the discovery-vs-validation
scatter ("4-quadrant") plots of ex vivo-stimulated cytokine production, across
the three pairwise endotype comparisons (All Low vs Mixed, Mixed vs All High,
All Low vs All High) and two stimulation durations (24 Hours, 7 Days), in the
2000HIV cohort (NCT03994835).

## Sheets
Six sheets are included, one per panel of the figure:

| Sheet name | Panel | Comparison | Stimulation |
|---|---|---|---|
| AllLow_vs_Mixed_24h | a (left) | All Low vs Mixed | 24 Hours |
| AllLow_vs_Mixed_7d | a (right) | All Low vs Mixed | 7 Days |
| Mixed_vs_AllHigh_24h | b (left) | Mixed vs All High | 24 Hours |
| Mixed_vs_AllHigh_7d | b (right) | Mixed vs All High | 7 Days |
| AllLow_vs_AllHigh_24h | c (left) | All Low vs All High | 24 Hours |
| AllLow_vs_AllHigh_7d | c (right) | All Low vs All High | 7 Days |

## Column definitions
Each sheet has one row per cytokine-stimulus combination.

- **Cytokine_Stimulus:** the cytokine and stimulus pair (e.g., "IL5 (PHA)"),
  as labeled in the figure.
- **Beta_Discovery:** normalized regression coefficient (β) from the
  Discovery cohort model. This is the x-axis value in the plot.
- **Pvalue_Discovery:** raw p-value from the Discovery cohort model.
- **FDR_Discovery:** Benjamini-Hochberg FDR-adjusted p-value from the
  Discovery cohort model. Used (at FDR<0.05) to define "Significant in
  discovery."
- **Beta_Validation:** normalized regression coefficient (β) from the
  Validation cohort model. This is the y-axis value in the plot.
- **Pvalue_Validation:** raw p-value from the Validation cohort model. Used
  (at P<0.05) to define "Significant in validation."
- **FDR_Validation** (where available): Benjamini-Hochberg FDR-adjusted
  p-value from the Validation cohort model.
- **Significance_Category:** the significance/color category assigned to
  each point in the plot, one of:
  - "Validated direction and discovery significance (P-value < 0.05)" — P-value<0.05 in Discovery AND
    with concordant effect direction in both Discovery and Validation cohorts
  - "Significant in discovery (P<0.05)" — P-value<0.05 in Discovery only
  - "Significant in validation (P<0.05)" — P-value<0.05 in Validation only
  - "Other" — none of the above

## Data processing
- Each cytokine-stimulus combination's β (normalized regression coefficient)
  and p-value were obtained from a separate linear regression model of
  cytokine concentration against endotype group, adjusted for Age, Sex,
  Season of Collection, Genetic PC1, COVID vaccination status, and Time to
  Laboratory Processing.
- Discovery and Validation cohort models were run independently, then joined
  by cytokine-stimulus variable.
- Significance classification uses p-values in the Discovery
  cohort and consistency of effect estimates in the Validation cohort, consistent with
  the two-stage discovery/validation design.
- Ex vivo cytokine production was measured after two stimulation durations
  (24 hours and 7 days), modeled and reported separately.

## Relationship to other source data
Sample-level cluster/endotype assignments used to define comparison groups
are provided in the Endotype_Label sheet of the multi-omics heatmap source
data file. Raw ex vivo cytokine production data are deposited in the Radboud
Data Repository (RDR); see the manuscript's Data Availability statement for
repository links.

